          <SubComponents>
            <Container class="javax.swing.JScrollPane" name="jScrollPane3">

              <Layout class="org.netbeans.modules.form.compat2.layouts.support.JScrollPaneSupportLayout"/>
              <SubComponents>
                <Component class="javax.swing.JTextArea" name="jTextArea3">
                  <Properties>
                    <Property name="columns" type="int" value="20"/>
                    <Property name="rows" type="int" value="5"/>
                    <Property name="text" type="java.lang.String" value="Loading Rule&#xa;1. Before loading Rule you must define your database was loaded.&#xa;2. If database didn&apos;t exist you can import/restore database using Restore procedure.&#xa;&#x9;- for Restoring prosedure: click menu Setting -  Restore Rule Database .&#xa;&#x9;- choose/browse your source sql direktori. ( you can choose Db-config-empty.sql for  empty &#x9;database configuration without contain rule)&#xa;&#x9;- after restoring empty database configuration, insert rule manually. The description of rule &#x9;insertion read instruction of Inserting Rule to database.&#xa;3. If you have defined your own last database sql file that contains rule, you can restoring that file.&#xa;(note : database structure must has same structure with this system, for details go to backup &amp; restore manual tab.)&#xa;4. After database was exist. You can click button load to displaying rule in the table Rule.&#xa;&#xa;Inserting Rule to Database&#xa;Inserting rule manually to database with parameter field:&#xa;- protocol &#x9;: network protocol ( tcp, udp or icmp)&#xa;- source ip&#x9;: source ip of network area&#xa;- source port&#x9;: source port used by services&#xa;- destination ip: destination ip of network area&#xa;- destination port: destination port of network that service running and port opened&#xa;- action&#x9;: action of decision when packet arrived to interface"/>
                  </Properties>
                </Component>
              </SubComponents>
            </Container>
          </SubComponents>
        </Container>
